course: dictionary
lesson: 13990
title: The word longest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long means a great distance from one end to the other, or a great amount of time. Longer compares two things. Longest picks out the one that is more long than all the others.
explain: «The blue pencil is long, the red one is longer, and the green one is the longest.» Notice the pattern: long, longer, longest. We add -est to show the most.
explain: Longest can also be about time. «The winter nights were the longest I can remember.» Here it means lasting the most time, not measuring a length.
fact: Longest is the superlative of long.
fact: The pattern is long, longer, longest.
fact: Use longest when you compare three or more things.
fact: «Longest» means more long than all the others.
fact: «Longest» can be about length, as in «the longest bridge», or about time, as in «the longest wait».
exercise: «Sam's rope is the longest in the gym.» What does longest mean here? | Shorter than the other ropes | Thickest of all the ropes | Heaviest of all the ropes | *Longer than all the other ropes
exercise: «This is the ___ bridge in the city.» Choose the right word. | *longest | short | longer | long
exercise: Which word is the superlative of long? | bigger | *longest | lengthy | longer
test: «Winter is the longest season for Ben, because the nights never seem to end.» What does longest mean here? | Most fun | Most snowy | *Lasting the most time | Coldest
test: «Of the three ribbons, the red one is the ___.» Which word fits? | longer | lengthy | long | *longest
exam: Which sentence uses longest correctly? | Our race was longest than yours | He is more longest than me | The rope is longest than the chain | *We walked the longest path in the park
